  "findings": [
    "CustomMttWebView constructor registers X5WebViewEventHandler via setWebViewClientExtension; handler has non-standard extension/touch/scroll callbacks, recorded separately from standard Client/Chrome canonical signatures. Its constructor also registers WebViewCallbackClient; do not silently ignore extension surface.",
    "CustomMttWebView ctor removes three legacy interface names; h.G additionally removes searchBoxJavaBridge conditional SDK path. Historical QQLive registration retained.",
    "CustomWebViewWrapper.d removes QQLive interface before and after delayed about:blank reset; this is lifecycle removal, not grounds to delete earlier bridge registration.",
    "H5InteractStandardActivity and FullScreenActivity own overrides only change layout/bind H5InteractView; H5InteractView overrides JSAPI provider and touch dispatch, not standard installed Client/Chrome setters. H5BaseActivity shared initialization and complete custom activity ancestry still require final review.",
    "SDK WebView.setWebViewClient selects X5 proxy i or native SystemWebViewClient; Chrome selects h, SystemWebChromeClient or class c. These SDK adaptation paths must be traced before whole wrapper callback closure."
  ]
